From: Peter M. <petermm@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Follow ESP-IDF software coexistence from the Wi-Fi OS table

ESP-IDF's Wi-Fi adapter calls coex_init(), coex_enable() and the request,
release, channel, duration, priority and scheme entry points when software
coexistence is enabled. The previous RTEMS entries matched the disabled
wrappers and always reported that Wi-Fi owned the radio.

Register the coexistence OS adapter and run coex_pre_init() before
esp_wifi_init_internal(), which is what ESP-IDF's secondary init function does
before esp_wifi_init(). The Wi-Fi blob registers its scheme callback before it
calls the OS adapter's _coex_init, so doing this from _coex_init is too late:
coex_schm_lock() reads the ROM data that coex_pre_init() fills in.
Scheme callbacks are stored and forwarded. Flexible-period entry points stay
at the disabled-wrapper values because CONFIG_ESP_COEX_POWER_MANAGEMENT is off.
libcoexist.a logs through coexist_printf, the same redirect the other radio
blobs already use.

libcoexist.a marks radio-arbitration helpers .coexiram. They run while the
flash cache may be off, same as the Wi-Fi IRAM sections, so they belong in
the resident Wi-Fi section rather than the unexpected-section catch-all.

